WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.680
Yusaku Maezawa please come forward.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.880
Space X’s first moon tourist, the 43 year
old Yusaku Maezawa, is an online retail tycoon

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.880
in Japan.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.390
He’s also controversial, often portrayed
negatively in Japanese media for flaunting

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:18.910
his wealth on social media.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.170
And he likes to dabble.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:25.940
He’s a punk rock drummer... turned entrepreneur
billionaire... turned art collector...

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.420
turned moon tourist.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.599
And his secret to success:

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.360
Work Less.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.430
This is how Yusaku Maezawa made billions by
dodging cultural norms in Japan, grabbing

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.980
publicity through outrageous purchases and
stunts.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.120
Maezawa’s recent purchase got him international
attention for the first time:

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.900
A round trip ticket to the moon on Space X’s
new rocket called "Starship", which is being

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.290
designed to colonize mars.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:04.470
He is, I think, the bravest person and most
willing to do so.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.300
Although he wouldn’t disclose the price
he’s paying for the ride, Elon Musk said

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:14.100
Yusaku is funding a material percentage of
Starship's estimated $5 billion development cost.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.300
At some point he began to talk with Elon Musk
about traveling to outer space.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.850
We don't know the exact timeline, but he is
the first passenger, he will be the first

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.670
private citizen to fly.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:30.260
Dubbed the dear moon project, Yusaku says
he will take artists and musicians of his

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.130
choice to, in his words, “inspire world
peace."

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.470
I do think this a really big publicity stunt
for Zozo.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.630
Zozo is Yusaku’s online clothing company.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:43.110
It’s what’s made him a billionaire in
his mid-30s.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.500
Maezawa has said publicly, that he wants to
become one of the top brands globally.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:56.240
He expects to quintuple his market cap right
now, to 50 billion dollars, within ten years.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.880
And a lot of that will be driven by global
expansion.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.750
These ambitious plans are in contrast to his
humble upbringing.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.020
His dad was an accountant and his mom a housewife.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:11.920
In a country known for conformity, Yusaku
Maezawa has always sought to stand out.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.270
It started in high school where he saw gloomy
white collared workers, called “salarymen”

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:17.980
in Japan, commuting to work.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:25.600
I always saw salarymen looking so unenthusiastic
on the train.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:31.420
That made me disheartened.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.460
He 
skipped college, spent time in California

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:38.840
and later joined a punk rock band called Switch
Style, which became popular within Japan.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:46.980
When asked why he became a drummer, he said
it's not so much that he loved playing on

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.940
the drums, it was just easier to join a band
as a drummer, because drummers

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.500
were in higher demand.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.440
You gotta start to see a pattern emerge that
he's a commercially, kind of transactionally

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.580
driven person, even from an early age.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:04.989
Shortly after joining the band, he started
his company “Start Today” which sold imported

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:07.880
records via mail order in Japan.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.790
Start Today became quite successful in selling
records, and then moved on into clothes.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:18.840
Yusaku was able to choose good music and good
clothes to sell online, which is how the business

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.209
began to take off.

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:25.770
The online clothing website, called “Zozotown,”
is now Japan’s go-to site for online fashion shopping.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.780
In 2010 when profits started to really, really
go up, and the company was approaching a billion

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:35.849
dollar market cap, he came out to an earnings
press conference, in front of analysts and

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:38.960
investors, and he was dressed like a giant
mushroom.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.740
It was one of his first times to kind of grab
the spotlight.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.700
And his attention grabbing stunts have been
getting increasingly controversial over the

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.700
past few years.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:52.650
His social-media feeds are full of French
wines, private jets, supercars, a Pablo Picasso

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.920
painting he purchased, and record-breaking
works from American street artist

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.640
Jean Michel Basquiat.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.459
The local media here is pretty relentless
in how they attack him.

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:09.160
They say that he shows off his money, he stands
for all the things that traditional Japanese

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.019
values, do not stand for.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.940
Younger people generally love him.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.560
They like someone who's open, they like that
he's extremely active on social media.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.060
Anytime I make a purchase, people just talk
about the price and that I have so much money…

00:04:21.069 --> 00:04:25.370
but in fact i’m buying the passion and the
history.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:31.370
Yusaku said he plans to make Zozo a leading
global clothing brand within a decade by revolutionizing

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:36.290
how people buy clothes online, beginning with
this year’s debut of a body-measuring outfit

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.849
called the Zozosuit.

00:04:37.849 --> 00:04:42.260
The Zozosuit has allowed Maezawa to collect
measurements of millions of people.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:47.270
He says he can now predict the perfect clothing
sizes from their sex, age, height and weight.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.240
He plans to use that to become a world-leading
clothing brand.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.330
I mean not even Amazon has released anything
like this, and they're the global e-commerce

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:01.949
leader and what better what to promote it
than to jump on Elon Musk's rocket around

00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:05.710
the moon so that everyone in the world knows
who Yusaku Maezawa is?

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.729
In order to stay ahead of the curve, Zozotown
is offering tech talent salaries of up to

00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:15.349
100 million yen which is an unusual move in
Japan, where workers often take lower pay

00:05:15.349 --> 00:05:17.309
in exchange for secure employment.

00:05:17.309 --> 00:05:22.680
He’s also encouraging employees to condense
work and spend more time outside the office

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.849
pursuing all kinds of intellectual and artistic
pursuits.

00:05:25.849 --> 00:05:30.889
I think Yusaku's secret is that he knows what
people want.

00:05:30.889 --> 00:05:33.169
He just kind of gets it.

00:05:33.169 --> 00:05:38.319
Whether Zozotown’s new technology revolutionizes
the way we shop online or not, the world will

00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:44.690
have its eyes on Yusaku and Elon Musk in 2023,
which is the estimated travel date for the

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.319
first ever tourist trip to the moon.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.500
As far as me going, I’m not sure…

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.340
Maybe we’ll both be on it.

